# Generated by `npm run openapi:snapshot`, which writes them with
# JSON.stringify(spec, null, 2). Prettier collapses short arrays onto one
# line, so formatting these files makes `npm run openapi:check` fail.
#
# Two of them: the API contract is edition-specific, and the second is the
# community spec the overlay publishes in place of this tree's.
docs/api/openapi.v1.json

# Claude Code worktrees under the primary checkout. Git hides them via
# .git/info/exclude, which Prettier does not read — so a format:check run in
# the primary checkout otherwise scans every worktree's full tree, where the
# anchored ignores above (e.g. docs/api/openapi.v1.json) do not match the
# nested copies and even a pristine worktree fails the scan. It also keeps
# `npm run format` from rewriting files inside live worktrees. CI checkouts
# never contain these.
.claude/worktrees/
